# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Python bytecode from the bundled workers
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Logs & temp
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
.playwright-mcp/

# Generated artifacts (written into target projects, not this repo)
.twt-artifacts/
/dist-codex/
/doc-hub-xivic/
# /twt-skill-test run output — reproducible per run; tracking it would dirty
# the tree after every run and block the NEXT --fix run's git guard.
tests/skill-test-runs/
/doc-landing/
# Redundant with .twt-artifacts/ above, but explicit: a test run against the
# launch-audit fixtures must never leave generated output tracked, even if
# the global rule above is ever narrowed.
tests/fixtures/*/.twt-artifacts/

# Local Claude Code settings & docs
.claude/settings.local.json
/docs/

# Subagent-driven-development scratch (ledger, task reports, review packages)
.superpowers/

# Agent instructions for THIS repo, kept local. Anchored with a leading slash:
# unanchored, `AGENTS.md` matches at any depth, and it silently dropped
# plugins/twt-wiki/templates/wiki/AGENTS.md - a file the wiki unit ships - out
# of every commit, so a fresh clone failed `build-units --check` on it.
# templates/wiki/AGENTS.md is plugin CONTENT (copied verbatim into every
# scaffolded .project-wiki/) and is tracked, along with its vendored copies.
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md

# Local environment / secrets
.env
.env.local
# ...except the launch-audit dirty fixture's intentionally-committed decoy —
# a fake, clearly-labeled placeholder value the HYG001 rule is supposed to
# trip on, not a real secret. Without this negation the global .env rule
# above silently drops it from every commit, and the fixture stops proving
# what it claims to prove.
!tests/fixtures/launch-dirty/.env

# Node dependencies are installed, never committed.
node_modules/
# package.json and package-lock.json ARE committed: package.json declares the
# marketplace's own playwright dependency, which tools/lib/resolve-playwright.mjs
# tries before the project and global installs, and it carries the `npm test`
# script. Without them a fresh clone can never install what the screenshot,
# fidelity and design-system-audit skills need.
# ...except the inherit-scan target fixtures (tests/fixtures/inherit-*),
# which model host codebases the scanner reads facts from — without a real
# package.json committed, scanProject would have nothing to read and the
# dependency/script/packageManager assertions in tests/inherit-scan.test.mjs
# would be exercising an empty object on every fresh clone or CI checkout.
!tests/fixtures/inherit-next-tailwind/package.json
!tests/fixtures/inherit-vite-modules/package.json
!tests/fixtures/inherit-monorepo/package.json
!tests/fixtures/inherit-monorepo/apps/web/package.json
!tests/fixtures/inherit-monorepo/apps/admin/package.json
!tests/fixtures/inherit-scss-aliases/package.json
# ...and the inherit-scan fixture's throwaway node_modules file, which
# proves the scanner's directory walk actually skips node_modules rather
# than vacuously passing a "no leaked files" assertion because the file
# was never there to leak in the first place (see the "walk skips
# node_modules, dist, and dot-directories" test).
!tests/fixtures/inherit-next-tailwind/node_modules/
!tests/fixtures/inherit-next-tailwind/node_modules/junk-pkg/
!tests/fixtures/inherit-next-tailwind/node_modules/junk-pkg/index.js
